id: pm-gh1475
title: "GH-1475: settle authenticated lossless merges within one reviewed delivery"
description: Published 2026.10.14 losslessly merges disjoint scalar edits and union collections but leaves a pending receipt and gate-failing health until explicit reconcile plus a second commit. Evaluate a complete audited settlement path that preserves existing evidence authentication and genuine conflicting-value review requirements.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-14T22:04:28.563Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-18T18:44:09.896Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-18T18:44:08.870Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-18T18:44:08.870Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "Reproduce the submitted fresh Git merge on the immutable published artifact and candidate; preserve both branch values and history; validate authenticated no-discard settlement and fresh-clone receipt portability; prove same-field conflicts, lossy decisions, malformed or unsealed legacy evidence remain review-required; retain SDK/CLI parity and non-surprising opt-in hook behavior; do not weaken health or verification merely to suppress a pending state."
parent: pm-dj98
risk: high
confidence: medium
severity: medium
resolution: "SDK guarded staging and the opt-in merge-aware hook settle lossless merges in one commit. Audit writes require matching immutable Git-index receipt proof, read-only previews expose valid unstaged candidates, and failed apply reverts only new receipt index entries. CLI/MCP contracts, lifecycle staging, documentation and real-Git compatibility evidence share the same SDK primitives."
expected_result: Lossless merges settle in one reviewed merge commit whose history and receipt evidence survive a fresh clone; unsafe cases refuse before audit writes and preserve operator staging.
actual_result: "The final linked58+14+19 tests passed, LF/CRLF and Bun single-commit fresh-clone journeys passed, receipt/staging exact coverage passed, and packed npm/npx/Bun consumers passed for9 packages. Static source/contract/assurance, typecheck and mutation checks passed. Local latency measurements exceeded limits under high load, including one unqualified bare-Node control; unchanged hosted static/timing and exact whole-repository coverage remain mandatory before merge."
